================================================================================
2. THE DATA  —  Retrosheet
================================================================================

Applies to the Retrosheet files fetched into data/retrosheet/ and to everything
derived from them, including retro.sqlite and the JSON in fixtures/.

    The information used here was obtained free of charge from and is
    copyrighted by Retrosheet. Interested parties may contact Retrosheet at
    "www.retrosheet.org".

That notice is Retrosheet's one condition, and it must appear prominently in
anything built on this data. It is carried in the page footer and on the About
page for that reason, not as decoration. Do not remove it.

Retrosheet's terms are otherwise unusually permissive, and notably more so than
the CC BY-SA 3.0 that governs the Lahman database used by the sibling
baseball-records repository. Recipients are free to make any desired use of the
information, including selling it, giving it away, or producing a commercial
product based upon it. There is no share-alike obligation, so the MIT grant in
section 1 stands on its own and derived work need not be relicensed.

Accuracy
--------
Retrosheet makes no guarantees of accuracy. From their notice:

    Much effort is expended to make our website as correct as possible, but
    Retrosheet shall not be held responsible for any consequences arising from
    the use of the material presented here. All information is subject to
    corrections as additional data are received. We are grateful to anyone who
    discovers discrepancies and we appreciate learning of the details.

This matters more here than it would for a season-totals database. Retrosheet
ships no season or career totals of its own; every total this app shows is
summed from individual game lines, and Retrosheet itself documents where its
box scores differ from the official record (see the discrepancies/ folder of
the distribution). Numbers here will therefore disagree with other sources in
places. The About page says so.

Changes made to the original data
---------------------------------
retro.sqlite is a modified derivative, not a verbatim copy:

  * Negative stat values, which Retrosheet uses to mean "not recorded", are
    stored as NULL so that summing does not subtract them.
  * Pinch-hit records are kept in a separate table from batting lines, because
    they annotate rather than add to them.
  * Kansas City Athletics game-log rows for 1955-1967 are recoded from OAK to
    KC1, matching every other file in the distribution.
  * Line scores are normalised to one comma-separated form.
  * Headers for Negro League games, which the game logs do not cover, are
    synthesised from the box-score files.

The files in data/retrosheet/ are unmodified as distributed by Retrosheet.
